              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="card glass">
            <div class="tag">Apps</div>
            <h3>App cleanup</h3>
            <p>
              Already have an app that's slow, buggy or out of date? We clean it up instead of
              starting over.
            </p>
            <ul>
              <li>Fix broken screens, sign-ins and checkout flows</li>
              <li>Speed it up and update the design</li>
              <li>Connect it to your dashboard and workflows</li>
            </ul>
            <div class="prices">
              <div>
                <b>$1,500–$4,000</b><span>Typical range. Fixed quote after a free review of your app</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 PRICING -->
    <section id="pricing" style="padding-top:20px">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="label">04 · Pricing</div>
          <h2>What it usually costs.</h2>
          <p class="sub">
            Every business needs something different, so these are typical ranges. Yours could come
            in lower or higher. After your free audit you get a fixed quote before any work starts.
          </p>
          <span class="pill">Founding clients · pricing toward the low end</span>
        </div>
        <div class="plans">
          <div class="plan glass">
            <div class="tag">Starter</div>
            <h3>Dashboard + 1 workflow</h3>
            <div class="price"><span class="typ">Typically</span>$400–$800</div>
            <div class="mo">Optional care: around $49/mo</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Your custom dashboard</li>
              <li>1 automation, such as booking + reminders</li>
              <li>Yours to keep, no monthly fee required</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="btn" href="#contact">Get a quote</a>
          </div>
          <div class="plan glass hot">
            <div class="tag">Most popular</div>
            <h3>Dashboard + 3 workflows</h3>
            <div class="price"><span class="typ">Typically</span>$1,000–$1,800</div>
            <div class="mo">Optional care: around $99/mo</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Your custom dashboard</li>
              <li>3 automations</li>
              <li>Weekly numbers email</li>
              <li>Yours to keep, no monthly fee required</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#contact">Get a quote</a>
          </div>
          <div class="plan glass">
            <div class="tag">Growth</div>
            <h3>Dashboard + up to 5 workflows</h3>
            <div class="price"><span class="typ">Typically</span>$1,800–$3,000</div>
            <div class="mo">Optional care: around $179/mo</div>
            <ul>
              <li>Your custom dashboard</li>
              <li>Up to 5 automations</li>
              <li>With care: 1 new workflow each month</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="btn" href="#contact">Get a quote</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="carenote">
          Care is optional. It covers the texts your workflows send, the software behind them,
          monitoring, fixes when a connected app changes, and small tweaks. Skip it and we set
          everything up on your own accounts, so you pay those small usage costs directly. Add or
          cancel care anytime.
        </p>
        <div class="fine">
          <span>
            <b>Websites</b> typically $300–$1,200, or $0 down around $59/mo · <b>App cleanup</b>
            typically $1,500–$4,000
          </span>
          <a href="#web">See websites &amp; apps →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 PROCESS -->
    <section id="process">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="label">05 · Process</div>
          <h2>Three steps.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step">
            <div class="dot">01</div>
            <h3>Free audit</h3>
            <p>We visit, see how your day runs, and find what to automate.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step on">
            <div class="dot">02</div>
            <h3>Working demo</h3>
            <p>You try your dashboard and workflows before you pay.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="step">
            <div class="dot">03</div>
            <h3>Launch</h3>
            <p>It goes live. Add care if you want us to keep watch.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 06 WORKING WITH US -->
    <section id="working" style="padding-top:20px">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="head">
          <div class="label">06 · Working with us</div>
          <h2>Real people, not a ticket queue.</h2>
          <p class="sub">You'll always know who to call, and you'll get a straight answer.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="ways">
          <div class="way glass">
            <div class="ic" aria-hidden="true">◎</div>
            <h3>We come to you</h3>
            <p>Your audit happens at your business, on your schedule, so we see how your day really runs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="way glass">
            <div class="ic" aria-hidden="true">✆</div>
            <h3>A direct line</h3>
            <p>Call or text the people doing the work. No call centers, no support tickets.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="way glass">
            <div class="ic" aria-hidden="true">¶</div>
            <h3>Plain language</h3>
            <p>No tech jargon. We explain what we're building, why, and what it costs before we start.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="way glass">
            <div class="ic" aria-hidden="true">↻</div>
            <h3>We check in</h3>
            <p>After launch, we check in to see what's working and what to add to your dashboard next.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CONTACT -->
    <section id="contact" class="contact">
      <div class="wrap">
        <div class="label c">Get started</div>
        <h2>Book your free audit.</h2>
        <p class="sub">
          30 minutes at your business. No obligation. Tell us what you would like built so we can
          prep before we meet.
        </p>
        <!-- A real POST target, so the form still works if the script below
             fails to load. The script upgrades it to a fetch and keeps the
             visitor on the page. -->
        <form id="lead" class="glass" action={FORMSPREE_ENDPOINT} method="POST">
          <div class="two">
            <input
              id="f-name"
              name="name"
              placeholder="Your name"
              autocomplete="name"
              aria-label="Your name"
              required
            />
            <input
              id="f-business"
              name="business"
              placeholder="Business name"
              autocomplete="organization"
              aria-label="Business name"
              required
            />
          </div>
          <input
            id="f-contact"
            name="contact"
            placeholder="Email or phone"
            autocomplete="email"
            aria-label="Email or phone"
            required
          />
          <div class="two">
            <input
              id="f-site"
              name="website"
              placeholder="Website (optional)"
              autocomplete="url"
              inputmode="url"
              aria-label="Website, optional"
            />
            <input id="f-app" name="app" placeholder="App name (optional)" aria-label="App name, optional" />
          </div>
          <textarea
            id="f-msg"
            name="msg"
            rows="3"
            placeholder="What do you wish ran itself? Or what would you want on your dashboard?"
            aria-label="What do you wish ran itself?"></textarea>
          <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit">Book my free audit</button>
          <div id="formerr" role="alert">
            Add your name, business name and an email or phone so we can reach you.
          </div>
          <div id="thanks" role="status">
            <p>Got it — thanks. We'll be in touch shortly to set up your free audit.</p>
          </div>
        </form>
        <div class="direct">
          <div class="dline">
            <span class="dl">Call or text</span><a class="sel" id="c-phone" href="tel:+18189397964"
            >(818) 939-7964</a
            ><button class="copy" data-copy="(818) 939-7964" type="button">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <div class="dline">
            <span class="dl">Email</span><a class="sel" id="c-email" href="mailto:beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com"
            >beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com</a
            ><button class="copy" data-copy="beng@futureclaritytechnologies.com" type="button">Copy</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />

  <div class="callbar">
    <a class="btn" href="tel:+18189397964">Call (818) 939-7964</a>
    <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#contact">Free audit</a>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  // ---- in-page navigation -------------------------------------------------
  const header = document.querySelector('header')!;
  const reduce = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;

  function goTo(id: string) {
    let y = 0;
    if (id !== '#top') {
      const sec = document.querySelector(id);
      if (!sec) return false;
      // Boxed sections line up by the box, not the title inside it.
      const mark = sec.querySelector('.band, .label, h2') || sec;
      y = mark.getBoundingClientRect().top + window.pageYOffset - header.getBoundingClientRect().height - 16;
    }
    window.scrollTo({ top: Math.max(0, y), behavior: reduce ? 'auto' : 'smooth' });
    if (id === '#contact') {
      setTimeout(
        () => document.getElementById('f-name')?.focus({ preventScroll: true }),
        reduce ? 0 : 650
      );
    }
    return true;
  }

  document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const a = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('a[href^="#"]');
    if (!a) return;
    const id = a.getAttribute('href');
    if (!id || id.length < 2) return;
    if (goTo(id)) e.preventDefault();
  });

  // Highlight the section you are in.
  const links = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('nav a'));
  const secs = links.map((a) => document.querySelector(a.getAttribute('href') || ''));

  function mark() {
    const line = header.getBoundingClientRect().height + 40;
    let cur = -1;
    secs.forEach((s, i) => {
      if (s && s.getBoundingClientRect().top <= line) cur = i;
    });
    links.forEach((a, i) => {
      const on = i === cur;
      a.classList.toggle('on', on);
      if (on && window.innerWidth <= 900) {
        const n = a.parentNode as HTMLElement;
        const el = a as HTMLElement;
        const l = el.offsetLeft - 16;
        const outOfView =
          el.offsetLeft < n.scrollLeft || el.offsetLeft + el.offsetWidth > n.scrollLeft + n.clientWidth;
        if (Math.abs(n.scrollLeft - l) > 4 && outOfView) n.scrollTo({ left: l, behavior: 'auto' });
      }
    });
  }

  let ticking = false;
  window.addEventListener(
    'scroll',
    () => {
      if (ticking) return;
      ticking = true;
      requestAnimationFrame(() => {
        ticking = false;
        mark();
      });
    },
    { passive: true }
  );
  mark();

  // ---- copy buttons -------------------------------------------------------
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.copy').forEach((b) => {
    b.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const t = b.getAttribute('data-copy') || '';
      const done = () => {
        b.textContent = 'Copied';
        setTimeout(() => (b.textContent = 'Copy'), 1800);
      };
      try {
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(t).then(done, () => (b.textContent = 'Select it above'));
      } catch {
        b.textContent = 'Select it above';
      }
    });
  });

  // ---- lead form ----------------------------------------------------------
  // Supabase is used when both vars are present at build time; Formspree is
  // the fallback, and a native form POST is the last resort so a lead is
  // never silently dropped. See the note at the top of this page.
  const SUPABASE_URL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL;
  const SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY;
  const SUPABASE_TABLE = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SUPABASE_LEADS_TABLE || 'leads';

  const form = document.getElementById('lead') as HTMLFormElement | null;

  if (form) {
    const val = (id: string) => (document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement).value.trim();

    async function toSupabase(payload: Record<string, string>) {
      if (!SUPABASE_URL || !SUPABASE_ANON_KEY) return false;
      const res = await fetch(`${SUPABASE_URL}/rest/v1/${SUPABASE_TABLE}`, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          apikey: SUPABASE_ANON_KEY,
          Authorization: `Bearer ${SUPABASE_ANON_KEY}`,
          Prefer: 'return=minimal',
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      });
      return res.ok;
    }

    async function toFormspree(payload: Record<string, string>) {
      const res = await fetch(form!.action, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', Accept: 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify(payload),
      });
      return res.ok;
    }

    form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
      e.preventDefault();

      const required = ['f-name', 'f-business', 'f-contact'];
      const missing = required.filter((id) => {
        const el = document.getElementById(id) as HTMLInputElement;
        const empty = !el.value.trim();
        el.setAttribute('aria-invalid', empty ? 'true' : 'false');
        return empty;
      });

      const err = document.getElementById('formerr')!;
      const thanks = document.getElementById('thanks')!;

      if (missing.length) {
        err.style.display = 'block';
        thanks.style.display = 'none';
        document.getElementById(missing[0])?.focus();
        return;
      }
      err.style.display = 'none';

      const payload = {
        name: val('f-name'),
        business: val('f-business'),
        contact: val('f-contact'),
        website: val('f-site'),
        app: val('f-app'),
        msg: val('f-msg'),
      };

      const button = form.querySelector('button[type="submit"]') as HTMLButtonElement;
      button.disabled = true;

      try {
        const sent = (await toSupabase(payload)) || (await toFormspree(payload));
        if (!sent) throw new Error('submission rejected');
        form.querySelectorAll('input, textarea').forEach((f) => ((f as HTMLInputElement).value = ''));
        thanks.style.display = 'block';
        button.disabled = false;
      } catch {
        // Fall back to a plain browser POST rather than losing the enquiry.
        form.submit();
      }
    });
  }
</script>
